                <pb facs="0318" n="190" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg190"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 133.</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Porter to Mr.
                            Cheng Tsao Ju</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-09-17"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 17,
                        1885</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to apprise you of the
                    receipt of a letter from the War Department, of to-day’s date, saying that Col.
                    A. McD. McCook, and Lieut. S. W. Groesbeek, adjutant of the Sixth United States
                    Infantry, met Colonel Bee and his colleagues yesterday, the 16th instant, at
                    Ogden City, Utah, and left with them for Rock Springs, Wyoming Territory, to
                    investigate the recent assault upon the Chinese laborers in that vicinity.</p>
                <p>Accept, sir, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JAS. D. PORTER,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                        Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
